{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-04T18:15:59.802Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4b273145923a68729ab394ab","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.289","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-04T18:15:59.802Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-04T18:15:59.802Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","text":"PR #170: queued mutations are stamped with the broadcast account (persisted session store), target workspace and an idempotency key generated before the first network attempt; foreign, unknown-owner and logged-out records are never replayed or deleted, and surface MUTATIONS_BLOCKED with a visible explicit recovery action that adopts unknown-owner records for the current account (assigning a key first). Server: pm_idempotency_keys claims (account, key) atomically, replays stored outcomes, rejects a key reused for a different request (422), never stores transient 425/429 refusals, answers 409 outcome-unknown instead of re-executing a stale pending key, catches outcome-persist failures, indexes created_at and throttles the retention sweep. Implemented by the pi (GLM-5.3) and codex (gpt-6.1-sol) agents; review round 1 (12 Greptile + CodeQL findings) fixed test-first. Local release:check: 451/451 tests pass."}]}],"before_hash":"1202a771d5125ac984ae5bb6e2705d57a6adff8bcc37c6c75a445888e1693802","after_hash":"4252fdce7191aeba1f93c7977fffeee02e3aa55e57557d7b16a17b6f03148801","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}